diff --git a/documentation/admins/managing_features/rag_and_search.mdx b/documentation/admins/managing_features/rag_and_search.mdx
index 1c1a43f232..905b012f84 100644
--- a/documentation/admins/managing_features/rag_and_search.mdx
+++ b/documentation/admins/managing_features/rag_and_search.mdx
@@ -32,3 +32,25 @@ See [Chat Preferences](/admins/managing_features/chat) for the chat-level settin
 
 Users can narrow a search by source, Document Set, and date range in chat.
 Users can explore what Onyx indexed with [Internal Search](/overview/core_features/internal_search).
+
+## QEdge Beta grounded summaries
+
+This Beta deployment adds a knowledge-only route for Agents listed in `QEDGE_RAG_PERSONAS`.
+Ordinary questions and detailed analysis both use the configured Flash model.
+The model combines retrieved passages into a summary with inline source citations.
+It does not display raw excerpts as the answer.
+
+The route retrieves fresh documents for each request and preserves user permissions and Document Set filters.
+Previous assistant answers are not factual evidence.
+Follow-up questions can reuse the previous user question for context. If the index lacks relevant evidence,
+the response states that limitation. If summary generation fails,
+the response asks you to retry instead of displaying excerpts.
+
+Set `QEDGE_RAG_MODEL_PROVIDER` to the configured provider name. Set `QEDGE_RAG_SUMMARY_MODEL` to its model identifier,
+currently `deepseek-flash`. Set `QEDGE_RAG_MIN_RELEVANCE` to the dedicated reranker threshold; the default is `0.20`.
+The dedicated reranker requires an existing SiliconFlow provider. Without it, lexical relevance filtering applies.
+Only relevance scores are cached for 120 seconds. Answers and document access decisions are not cached.
+
+File attachments, Projects, incognito sessions, and multi-model conversations use the standard Onyx route.
+Remove an Agent ID from `QEDGE_RAG_PERSONAS` and restart the backend services to disable this custom route for that
+Agent.
